Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:16:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Hades II: bake the widescreen Lua fix into the RomFS at build
 time

The Hades II Lua bake (patch port 0074, group L of the port inventory), carried from the Tiaoge-tou/nxnative fork.

dm/tools/romfs_patch.py applies exact line replacements to text files inside a RomFS image or a loose RomFS folder, in place. Counts must match the spec exactly, in one of two states (wholly stock or wholly patched): a wholly patched file counts as already patched and is left alone, so extraction reuse never double-patches, and every other mismatch stops the build rather than patching another version's files.

The Hades II profile gains romfs_patch.tsv (the widescreen Lua fix: RunLogic's frame lookups, the HUD anchors, the trait tray and the objective start) and the romfs_patch row in game.tsv that names it.

scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py runs the tool on the packed version's extracted files right after the profile is settled, before anything reads the files or the image's identity is taken, so a separate-RomFS build's romfs.id names the patched image and every later build stamps the same identity for the image the player already holds. Profiles without the row build exactly as before.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Hades II widescreen Lua fix baked into the RomFS image at build time, identity taken after patching (PROJECT.md Phase 2)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

